IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sga2-nouns`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: s 76(5), (6) and (7) -- the offence a contravention of s 76(1) or (1A) creates for the officers in default,
-- the compensation order the Court may make on conviction, and the Court's power of relief under s 391.
-- Layer 1. The contravention is a fact the caller states (or derives with sga2-s76-prohibition.l4); this module does not restate s 76(1) or (1A).
-- Whether an officer is "in default" is asked as a fact: the Act's own definition of that expression is not in these ranges.

§ `Section 76(5): the offence of the officers in default`

-- (5): if a company contravenes (1) or (1A), the company shall not be guilty of an offence, despite section 407.
-- src:7412 | (5) If a company contravenes subsection (1) or (1A), the company
-- src:7413 | shall not be guilty of an offence, despite section 407, but each officer
-- src:7414 | of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence and
-- src:7415 | shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $20,000 or to
-- src:7416 | imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or to both.
@ref s 76(5) (src:7412-7416)
GIVEN `the company has contravened subsection (1) or (1A) of section 76` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(5) the company is guilty of an offence by contravening subsection (1) or (1A)` MEANS
    IF `the company has contravened subsection (1) or (1A) of section 76`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company shall not be guilty of an offence, despite section 407"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence speaks of a company that "contravenes subsection (1) or (1A)" and says nothing of a company that has not

-- (5): each officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence.
-- src:7412 | (5) If a company contravenes subsection (1) or (1A), the company
-- src:7413 | shall not be guilty of an offence, despite section 407, but each officer
-- src:7414 | of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence and
-- src:7415 | shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $20,000 or to
-- src:7416 | imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or to both.
@ref s 76(5) (src:7412-7416)
GIVEN `the company has contravened subsection (1) or (1A) of section 76` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(5) the officer is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF    `the company has contravened subsection (1) or (1A) of section 76`
      AND `the person is an officer of the company`
      AND `the officer is in default`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "each officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element of the offence is unmet; the provision's own question (split site (i), fork line F-A5)

-- (5): "a fine not exceeding $20,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or to both" (36 months).
-- src:7412 | (5) If a company contravenes subsection (1) or (1A), the company
-- src:7413 | shall not be guilty of an offence, despite section 407, but each officer
-- src:7414 | of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence and
-- src:7415 | shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $20,000 or to
-- src:7416 | imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or to both.
@ref s 76(5) (src:7412-7416)
GIVEN `the company has contravened subsection (1) or (1A) of section 76` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 76 penalty`
`s 76(5) the most the officer may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 76(5) the officer is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `the company has contravened subsection (1) or (1A) of section 76` `the person is an officer of the company` `the officer is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 76 penalty` OF 20000, 36, TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the officer it makes guilty

-- The prohibition derived from the offence (ruling N2 of 2026-11-04: where the text names the bearer, SHANT is derived): an officer of the company
-- must not be in default when the company contravenes (1) or (1A). No time limit: only the forbidden act reaches BREACH.
-- src:7412 | (5) If a company contravenes subsection (1) or (1A), the company
-- src:7413 | shall not be guilty of an offence, despite section 407, but each officer
-- src:7414 | of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence and
-- src:7415 | shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $20,000 or to
-- src:7416 | imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or to both.
@ref s 76(5) (src:7412-7416)
GIVEN `the name of the officer` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 76 act`
`s 76(5) an officer of the company must not be in default when the company contravenes subsection (1) or (1A)` MEANS
    PARTY Officer `the name of the officer`
    SHANT `s 76(5) be an officer of the company who is in default when the company contravenes subsection (1) or (1A)`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Officer `the name of the officer` BECAUSE "the officer was in default when the company contravened section 76(1) or (1A)"

§ `Section 76(6): compensation on conviction`

-- (6): where a person is convicted of an offence under (5) and the Court is satisfied that the company or another person has suffered loss or damage as a result
-- of the contravention that constituted the offence, the Court may, in addition to the penalty, order the convicted person to pay compensation.
-- src:7420 | (6) Where a person is convicted of an offence under subsection (5)
-- src:7421 | and the Court by which the person is convicted is satisfied that the
-- src:7422 | company or another person has suffered loss or damage as a result of
-- src:7423 | the contravention that constituted the offence, that Court may, in
-- src:7424 | addition to imposing a penalty under that subsection, order the
-- src:7425 | convicted person to pay compensation to the company or other person
-- src:7426 | (as the case may be) of such amount as the Court specifies, and any
-- src:7427 | such order may be enforced as if it were a judgment of the Court.
@ref s 76(6) (src:7420-7427)
GIVEN `the person is convicted of an offence under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied that the company or another person has suffered loss or damage as a result of the contravention that constituted the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(6) the Court may order the convicted person to pay compensation` MEANS
    IF    `the person is convicted of an offence under subsection (5)`
      AND `the Court is satisfied that the company or another person has suffered loss or damage as a result of the contravention that constituted the offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person is convicted of an offence under subsection (5) and the Court ... is satisfied that ... loss or damage" -- a "may" function gated by "where": periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); listed in group G1 (fork line F-A6), the other reading is NOTHING (the grant rule of 2026-11-12)

-- (6): "any such order may be enforced as if it were a judgment of the Court".
-- src:7420 | (6) Where a person is convicted of an offence under subsection (5)
-- src:7421 | and the Court by which the person is convicted is satisfied that the
-- src:7422 | company or another person has suffered loss or damage as a result of
-- src:7423 | the contravention that constituted the offence, that Court may, in
-- src:7424 | addition to imposing a penalty under that subsection, order the
-- src:7425 | convicted person to pay compensation to the company or other person
-- src:7426 | (as the case may be) of such amount as the Court specifies, and any
-- src:7427 | such order may be enforced as if it were a judgment of the Court.
@ref s 76(6) (src:7420-7427)
GIVEN `the order is an order to pay compensation made under subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(6) the order may be enforced as if it were a judgment of the Court` MEANS
    IF `the order is an order to pay compensation made under subsection (6)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any such order may be enforced as if it were a judgment of the Court" -- the sentence speaks of an order under (6) only

§ `Section 76(7): relief under section 391`

-- (7): the power of a Court under section 391 to relieve a person to whom that section applies extends to relieving a person against whom an order may be
-- made under (6) from the liability to have such an order made. Section 391 itself is not in these ranges.
-- src:7429 | (7) The power of a Court under section 391 to relieve a person to
-- src:7430 | whom that section applies, wholly or partly and on such terms as the
-- src:7431 | Court thinks fit, from a liability referred to in that section extends to
-- src:7432 | relieving a person against whom an order may be made under
-- src:7433 | subsection (6) from the liability to have such an order made against
-- src:7434 | the person.
@ref s 76(7) (src:7429-7434)
GIVEN `an order may be made against the person under subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(7) the power of the Court under section 391 extends to relieving the person from the liability to have an order made under subsection (6)` MEANS
    IF `an order may be made against the person under subsection (6)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "extends to relieving a person against whom an order may be made under subsection (6)" -- a scope limit with no "only" (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c))
